{"body": "Conjecture: open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle.recover_json_object gives the same answer on two replies that its documented rule requires it to tell apart. The rule says: \"The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text.\" Reply A is the text '```json\n{\"a\": 1}\n```\n```text\n{\"b\": 2}\n```'. Reply B is the text '```json\n{\"a\": 1}\n```'. For Reply A the rule requires the answer {'b': 2}, because the ```text fence holds an object and comes after the ```json fence, so the last object inside a code fence is {\"b\": 2}. For Reply B the rule requires {'a': 1}, because the only fenced object is {\"a\": 1}. The check, however, returns {'a': 1} for both: its fence regex matches only ```json, ```JSON, or untagged fences, so it ignores the ```text fence in Reply A and scores the earlier json-fenced object. What would make me wrong is an observation that the check returns {'b': 2} for Reply A and {'a': 1} for Reply B, or that the rule as written does not treat a ```text fence as a code fence."}